---
description: Rules for the voxel engine (src/engine)
globs: src/engine/**/*.ts
---

`src/engine/` never imports React or the store. Systems are small and single-purpose;
`core/Engine.ts` composes them on one game loop, each with its own try/catch so one
failing system cannot freeze the game.

Blocks: behaviour, shape, light, collision and textures live on the `BlockDefinition`
(`blocks/blocks.ts`). Never compare a block id to a string. Numeric ids are permanent.

World edits: always through a `Command` (`commands/`), so Undo removes them.

Playbooks: `docs/contributing/add-a-block.md`, `add-a-building.md`, `add-a-tool.md`.
